.TH GIT-UPDATE-REMOTE-BRANCHES 1 "2026-10-01" "Git Helpers" "git-helpers Manual"
.SH NAME
git-update-remote-branches \- push tracked branches to their configured remote
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git update-remote-branches
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBgit-update-remote-branches\fR scans the local branches, finds the remote that
should receive pushes, and pushes any branch whose tracking state is out of sync.
It uses \fBgit push --force-with-lease\fR and skips branches that have no remote
tracking branch configured.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B git update-remote-branches
Push all local branches that are ahead or behind their tracked remote.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-push (1)
